y:** 0.10  \n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 1.00  \n- **CAM explanation:** the model focused on a localized central area in the kidney image that may reflect structural alteration.\n\n### Tool-provided next steps\n- Further medical evaluation with imaging/labs to confirm what this lesion is.\n- Discuss the result with a medical professional.\n- Consider additional testing if your clinician thinks it is needed.\n\nThis output is a **preliminary signal, not an actual diagnosis**. Since a diagnostic tool has now run, if you want, I can next help you use the **LLM distillation tool** approach and turn this plus your symptoms/history into a clearer patient-facing report with suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_057c1d92677879510169ba8f63e8d4819196d205b90b01b44b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9295,"output":562,"cacheRead":16384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26241,"cost":{"input":0.0232375,"output":0.00843,"cacheRead":0.004096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.035763500000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773834077966}}
